WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:11.607
Robin Hood had killed a man and killed the king's deer.

2
00:00:11.608 --> 00:00:16.328
It was impossible for the young man to return home.

3
00:00:16.329 --> 00:00:22.035
So he became an outlaw living in Sherwood Forest.

4
00:00:22.036 --> 00:00:27.707
As the year passed, one hundred outlaws joined him in the woods.

5
00:00:27.708 --> 00:00:33.117
Some of these outlaws were in trouble for shooting the king's deer because they were hungry.

6
00:00:33.118 --> 00:00:38.048
Other men had lost their land when the king seized it for himself.

7
00:00:38.049 --> 00:00:42.313
Some men had been cheated by rich, evil bishops.

8
00:00:42.314 --> 00:00:46.929
So they were all forced to leave home and hide in the forest.

9
00:00:46.930 --> 00:00:55.234
In time they chose Robin as their leader, and like Robin, they vowed to help the poor and people in need.

10
00:00:55.235 --> 00:00:59.135
One spring morning Robin felt restless.

11
00:00:59.136 --> 00:01:02.371
He decided to look for adventure.

12
00:01:02.372 --> 00:01:07.497
"You stay behind in the woods and listen for my horn," he said to his men.

13
00:01:07.498 --> 00:01:10.983
"If I blow it three times, come running.

14
00:01:10.984 --> 00:01:14.880
It's a signal that I need your help."

15
00:01:14.881 --> 00:01:19.325
Robin wandered out of the forest.

16
00:01:19.326 --> 00:01:24.343
He greeted pretty girls on their way to market.

17
00:01:24.344 --> 00:01:30.082
He saw a monk riding a donkey and a knight on a fine horse.

18
00:01:30.083 --> 00:01:34.614
He bowed before a fair lady.

19
00:01:34.615 --> 00:01:38.454
At last he came to a narrow wooden bridge over a stream.

20
00:01:38.455 --> 00:01:42.335
He spotted a huge stranger on the other side.

21
00:01:42.336 --> 00:01:46.447
The narrow bridge was only wide enough for one man.

22
00:01:46.448 --> 00:01:50.302
Both men hurried to cross the bridge first.

23
00:01:50.303 --> 00:01:53.084
They met in the middle.

24
00:01:53.085 --> 00:01:56.083
"Out of my way!" cried Robin.

25
00:01:56.084 --> 00:02:01.424
"No," replied the stranger. "You get out of my way!"

26
00:02:01.425 --> 00:02:07.023
"I'll use my bow and arrows to make you move!" declared Robin.

27
00:02:07.024 --> 00:02:09.880
"You coward!" said the man.

28
00:02:09.881 --> 00:02:12.172
"You threaten me with a bow.

29
00:02:12.173 --> 00:02:14.766
But all I have is this."

30
00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:19.718
He shook a heavy wooden staff, the kind used for fighting.

31
00:02:19.719 --> 00:02:23.565
"No one calls me a coward!" said Robin.

32
00:02:23.566 --> 00:02:27.028
"I'll cut a staff from those trees over there.

33
00:02:27.029 --> 00:02:29.529
Then we'll see what happens!"

34
00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:33.788
Robin stepped off the bridge and made a long staff from a tree.

35
00:02:33.789 --> 00:02:37.527
While he worked, he sneaked a look at the stranger.

36
00:02:37.528 --> 00:02:42.887
The tall man was whistling and gazing at the stream as he waited for Robin.

37
00:02:42.888 --> 00:02:47.103
"That guy is huge!" Robin said to himself.

38
00:02:47.104 --> 00:02:50.412
"He looks quite strong too!"

39
00:02:50.413 --> 00:02:55.390
But Robin went bravely back to the bridge carrying his staff.

40
00:02:55.391 --> 00:03:00.817
"I'm ready. Let's fight on the bridge until one of us tumbles into the stream."

41
00:03:00.818 --> 00:03:06.832
The stranger twirled his staff over his head. "Let's go!"

42
00:03:06.833 --> 00:03:13.809
Robin struck first, but the stranger blocked the blow.

43
00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:20.139
After an hour both men were tired and bruised.

44
00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:24.512
At last Robin smacked the stranger in the ribs.

45
00:03:24.513 --> 00:03:27.637
The man wobbled, but didn't fall off the bridge.

46
00:03:27.638 --> 00:03:30.312
Instead he hit Robin over the head.

47
00:03:30.313 --> 00:03:32.593
Robin was furious!

48
00:03:32.594 --> 00:03:35.230
He hit the man as hard as he could.

49
00:03:35.231 --> 00:03:42.264
But the stranger struck back, knocking Robin into the stream.

50
00:03:42.265 --> 00:03:47.493
The stranger laughed. "And where are you now?"

51
00:03:47.494 --> 00:03:50.544
Robin couldn't help laughing too.

52
00:03:50.545 --> 00:03:55.989
"I'm floating out to sea!" he joked as he climbed onto dry land.

53
00:03:55.990 --> 00:04:00.173
"Let's shake hands. You're the bravest man I've ever met!"

54
00:04:00.174 --> 00:04:03.809
Robin raised his horn and blew three times.

55
00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:09.330
Suddenly a group of men dressed in green burst from the woods.

56
00:04:09.331 --> 00:04:12.140
"What's wrong, Robin?" called Will Scarlet.

57
00:04:12.141 --> 00:04:13.869
"You're soaking wet."

58
00:04:13.870 --> 00:04:18.836
Robin grinned. "This big fellow knocked me into the water."

59
00:04:18.837 --> 00:04:22.293
"Then he shall go for a swim too!" cried Will.

60
00:04:22.294 --> 00:04:25.606
Robin's men leaped onto the stranger.

61
00:04:25.607 --> 00:04:32.424
The stranger fought back fiercely with his staff, but they wrestled him to the ground.

62
00:04:32.425 --> 00:04:34.744
"Let him go!" Robin said.

63
00:04:34.745 --> 00:04:38.707
"Don't hurt him. He seems like a good and honest man."

64
00:04:38.708 --> 00:04:43.901
Then he said to the stranger, "How about joining my band of men?

65
00:04:43.902 --> 00:04:47.244
You'll have three suits of green clothes every year.

66
00:04:47.245 --> 00:04:50.192
Plus, all you can eat and drink."

67
00:04:50.193 --> 00:04:54.383
"You're not very good with a staff," grumbled the man.

68
00:04:54.384 --> 00:04:57.045
He was still angry with Robin's men.

69
00:04:57.046 --> 00:05:00.240
"Can you shoot an arrow better than I can?

70
00:05:00.241 --> 00:05:03.675
If so, then I'll join you."

71
00:05:03.676 --> 00:05:08.828
"Fine!" said Robin. "Someone lend this stranger a bow and arrow."

72
00:05:08.829 --> 00:05:13.717
Will cut a small piece of white bark and fastened it to a tree.

73
00:05:13.718 --> 00:05:15.906
The stranger took aim.

74
00:05:15.907 --> 00:05:18.632
He hit the bark with his first arrow.

75
00:05:18.633 --> 00:05:24.136
"Nice shot," Robin said. "Now it is my turn."

76
00:05:24.137 --> 00:05:27.064
Robin stepped up and aimed.

77
00:05:27.065 --> 00:05:32.710
His arrow cut through the air—and split the first arrow down the middle!

78
00:05:32.711 --> 00:05:37.140
"What an incredible shot!" cried the stranger.

79
00:05:37.141 --> 00:05:41.889
"I'm John Little, and I'll gladly join your band."

80
00:05:41.890 --> 00:05:49.097
Robin grinned. "You're such a big man—I think we'll call you Little John.

81
00:05:49.098 --> 00:05:54.765
My name is Robin Hood, and you shall be my right-hand man."

